From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 18:05:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] hid: trace relative input events

AfterDOS class selection binds the generic hid.class ahead of bootmouse.class,
so the bootmouse trace correctly remains silent.  Instrument the active class
at the equivalent boundary: report its accumulated relative deltas and the
result of submitting IND_WRITEEVENT to input.device.
---
 rom/usb/classes/hid/hid.class.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rom/usb/classes/hid/hid.class.c b/rom/usb/classes/hid/hid.class.c
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/rom/usb/classes/hid/hid.class.c
+++ b/rom/usb/classes/hid/hid.class.c
@@ -6424,7 +6424,14 @@ void nFlushEvents(struct NepClassHid *nch)
         nch->nch_InpIOReq->io_Data = &nch->nch_FakeEvent;
         nch->nch_InpIOReq->io_Length = sizeof(struct InputEvent);
         nch->nch_InpIOReq->io_Command = nch->nch_OS4Hack ? IND_ADDEVENT : IND_WRITEEVENT;
-        DoIO((struct IORequest *) nch->nch_InpIOReq);
+        bug("[HID:MOUSE] submit x=%ld y=%ld code=%04lx qual=%04lx cmd=%lu\n",
+            (LONG)nch->nch_FakeEvent.ie_X, (LONG)nch->nch_FakeEvent.ie_Y,
+            (ULONG)nch->nch_FakeEvent.ie_Code,
+            (ULONG)nch->nch_FakeEvent.ie_Qualifier,
+            (ULONG)nch->nch_InpIOReq->io_Command);
+        ioerr = DoIO((struct IORequest *) nch->nch_InpIOReq);
+        if(ioerr != 0)
+            bug("[HID:MOUSE] input.device failed: %ld\n", ioerr);
         nch->nch_NewMouseRel = FALSE;
         nch->nch_MouseDeltaX = 0;
         nch->nch_MouseDeltaY = 0;
